win32u: dump the whole swapchain create_info, and its pNext chain

Metro Redux and Resident Evil Requiem reach the driver call with identical
values in every field patches/wine/0025 prints:

    create_info copied, surface handle 0x…, extent 1920x1080, format 44
    caps current 1920x1080, min 1920x1080, max 1920x1080, images 3..0
    extent clamped to 1920x1080
    calling driver vkCreateSwapchainKHR

Metro gets a swapchain. Requiem faults inside the driver. Same surface, same
capabilities, same extent, same format, same clamp -- so whatever differs is a
field that was not being printed, and three cheap guesses have now been spent
on fields that turned out to be identical.

pNext is the first suspect and the reason the chain is walked rather than just
counted: vkd3d-proton attaches present-id and present-wait structures that DXVK
never sends, and a WSI that handles the plain path can fault on the extended
one. sType alone is enough -- the question is which structures are in the
chain, not what is in them.

The rest of the struct is printed for the same reason the capabilities were
added to 0025: an inference is not worth an hour of build time twice, and every
field left unprinted is another round trip.

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2700,6 +2700,39 @@
                    create_info_host.imageFormat );
     }
 
+    /* Vessel: everything the driver is actually given, and the pNext chain.
+     *
+     * The fields above were not enough. Metro Redux and Resident Evil Requiem
+     * reach here with the same surface, the same capabilities, the same
+     * 1920x1080 extent and the same format 44; Metro gets a swapchain and
+     * Requiem faults inside the driver. Whatever differs is in this struct and
+     * was not being printed, so all of it is printed now.
+     *
+     * pNext matters most: vkd3d-proton attaches present-id and present-wait
+     * structures that DXVK never sends, and a half-initialised WSI can handle
+     * the plain path and fault on the extended one. sType is printed rather
+     * than the contents because the identity of the chain is the question. */
+    TRACE( "  create_info minImageCount %u, format %u, colorSpace %u, arrayLayers %u\n",
+           create_info_host.minImageCount, create_info_host.imageFormat,
+           create_info_host.imageColorSpace, create_info_host.imageArrayLayers );
+    TRACE( "  create_info usage %#x, sharing %u, preTransform %#x, composite %#x\n",
+           create_info_host.imageUsage, create_info_host.imageSharingMode,
+           create_info_host.preTransform, create_info_host.compositeAlpha );
+    TRACE( "  create_info presentMode %u, clipped %u, flags %#x, oldSwapchain %p\n",
+           create_info_host.presentMode, create_info_host.clipped, create_info_host.flags,
+           (void *)(UINT_PTR)create_info_host.oldSwapchain );
+    {
+        const VkBaseInStructure *chain = create_info_host.pNext;
+        unsigned int depth = 0;
+        while (chain && depth < 16)
+        {
+            TRACE( "  create_info pNext[%u] sType %u\n", depth, chain->sType );
+            chain = chain->pNext;
+            depth++;
+        }
+        if (!depth) TRACE( "  create_info pNext empty\n" );
+    }
+
     TRACE( "  calling driver vkCreateSwapchainKHR\n" );
     if ((res = device->p_vkCreateSwapchainKHR( device->host.device, &create_info_host, NULL, &host_swapchain )))
     {
